INT. USC VANGUARD - PROPULSION DECK - 2182

The deep vibration of twin sub-light ion thrusters echoes through the deckplates.

CHIEF ENGINEER MARCUS VANCE (44) monitors the coolant flow on the main engineering manifold.

DR. ARIS THORNE (Model AX-9) approaches, carrying the weekly fleet status report.

DR. ARIS THORNE
Ion thruster calibration complete, Chief. We are cruising at zero-point-one-eight sub-light.

CHIEF ENGINEER MARCUS VANCE
Good. Ever since we lost the Hyperion Drive back in 2175, we rely on honest reaction mass. What is the status of the deep courier Borealis?

DR. ARIS THORNE
Sub-space telemetry confirms USC Borealis is on track. Agent Gabriel Cross is still safely asleep in cryogenic stasis pod 09. He has eight years remaining before his scheduled revival in 2190.

CHIEF ENGINEER MARCUS VANCE
Let him sleep. Out here, patience is the only thing keeping us breathing.
